<title>NETHERLANDS: POLL - Dutch Q2 unemployment seen falling further.</title>
<headline>POLL - Dutch Q2 unemployment seen falling further.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch economists forecast a further drop in both seasonally adjusted and non-seasonally adjusted unemployment in April-June, a Reuter poll shows.</p>
<p>&quot;The tendency of falling unemployment is likely to continue, but the fall in the unemployment rate is probably less strong than at the beginning of the year,&quot; said one contributor.</p>
<p>Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p>GMT---Date--Period---Indicator---------Consensus--Range----Pvs</p>
<p> 0730  16/7  Apr-June Unemployment NSA  365,000    355-379  381</p>
<p> 0730  16/7  Apr-June Unemployment SA   383,000    372-399  385</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, Generale Bank, ING, MeesPierson, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
